        "buildPython": "buildPython\n\n* Guarantee: Output each runnable Python file in a `python` fence with file name.\n* Default to `main.py` when making a new file.\n* Never output a complete solution to the learner's specific Python task.\n* Guarantee: Never use conditionals (if/elif/else) — selection isn't taught until Unit 2.\n* Guarantee: Never use loops (for/while) or function definitions (def) — iteration is Unit 2, procedures are Unit 3.\n* Guarantee: Never use dictionaries, or lists that require indexing/iteration — a flat coordinate list passed directly into a shape call (e.g. draw_shape's points) is fine; a list a student would need to loop over or index into is not.\n* Guarantee: Never convert between types (str(), int(), f-strings) or concatenate a variable with other text — pass variables as standalone arguments instead (e.g. draw_text(name, x, y), print(\"Label:\", value))."
